    {
      "id": "b2",
      "function": "problem",
      "scene_type": "rv_cutaway",
      "spoken": "Combustion takes time. So the plug fires before top dead centre, and the highest pressure hits the piston just after it. As an example, the engineering lecture gives thirty degrees before top dead centre. That gives the flame time to spread before the piston moves away.",
