    {
      "id": "b4",
      "function": "demonstration",
      "scene_type": "rv_board",
      "spoken": "According to the lecture, the curve around the optimum is flat. Five to seven degrees late costs only about one percent of torque. Too early, heat losses and the tendency to knock go up. Too late, work is wasted.",
