    {
      "id": "b5",
      "function": "insight",
      "scene_type": "rv_cutaway",
      "spoken": "To keep the engine out of knock, a knock sensor on the crankcase listens in. When it detects knock, the control unit adjusts the spark timing, as Bosch describes it. That keeps the engine below its knock limit.",
